Live on your management cluster: demo-resources. Each variant's profile deploys the same add-ons to the same cluster, and Sveltos lets one profile manage a release at a time, so the per-cluster profiles wait until the live one steps aside. apply also writes takeover.sh, which hands each release over without reinstalling it; run it after apply.sh. See "If your profiles are live" in docs/user/onboard-your-sveltos-fleet.md.


Wrote onboard/apply.sh and the files it reads. Read it, then run it:
  MGMT_CONTEXT=<kubectl context of your management cluster> bash onboard/apply.sh

Then hand the live profiles over, without reinstalling anything:
  MGMT_CONTEXT=<same context> bash onboard/takeover.sh
  policyRefs:
  - deploymentType: Remote
    force: false
    kind: ConfigMap
    name: demo-resources
    namespace: default
    optional: false

